@@ -417,6 +417,15 @@ sandbox workload directly. The relay supports:
 - Tar-based file sync.
 - Port forwarding where supported by the CLI/TUI surface.
 
+Before dropping identity, full-mode canonical and independent PTY children
+transfer their freshly allocated slave descriptor to the same resolved UID/GID
+used for execution, with owner-only mode 0600. They never chown a workload
+pathname or grant membership in the supervisor's terminal group. A failed
+transfer aborts spawn. Filesystem policy must separately allow the terminal
+paths a workload needs. Linux policy preparation opens path-only, close-on-exec
+descriptors through rustix, including device paths such as `/dev/tty`; it does
+not activate devices or require the parent to have a controlling terminal.
+
 Sandbox logs are emitted locally and can also be pushed back to the gateway.
 Security-relevant sandbox behavior uses OCSF structured events; internal
 diagnostics use ordinary tracing.
